Statement of changes, as CC BY-SA 4.0 requires
----------------------------------------------

This is **not** a verbatim copy. `scripts/build_cskg_kg.py` projects CSKG down
to a small subgraph and the selection rule is stated in full there and in
`symbolic_ai_kg/_vendor.py::CSKG_SELECTION`. In summary, the derived file:

  * keeps only English ConceptNet-style concept nodes whose lemma is a single
    lowercase alphabetic word, collapsed by lemma rather than by sense;
  * keeps ten of the fifty-eight relations, renaming them onto this repo's own
    relation names (`IsA` -> `isa`, `HasProperty` and `MayHaveProperty` ->
    `property`, `HasA` and reversed `PartOf` -> `part`, `MadeOf` ->
    `substance`, `CapableOf` -> `can`, plus `similar` and `antonym`);
  * drops `RelatedTo` and `Synonym` entirely;
  * adds two fields CSKG does not have — a part-of-speech tag and a WordNet-
    style lexicographer name — both **derived by this repo** from the graph's
    own `isa` closure, not asserted by CSKG. See the module docstring of
    `scripts/build_cskg_kg.py`, which says so plainly, because a derived
    judgement presented as upstream data would be an attribution error as well
    as a research one.

Because CSKG is ShareAlike, this derived subset is offered under the same
CC BY-SA 4.0 license.
